doc Conditional: if cond ... [else ...] end
  Runs the first block if the condition is non-zero, otherwise the `else`
  block, if there is one.

  ```
  if n % 15 == 0
    print "FizzBuzz"
  else
    if n % 3 == 0
      print "Fizz"
    else
      print n
    end
  end
  ```

  There is no `else if` chain yet; nest `if` inside `else` instead.

syntax statement
  if {cond: expr int} {then: block} [else {else: block}] end
